## Fixes

### Fix 1: tryAAConformanceSuffix — structured S<letter>R<subject>rl requirement parsing (+8)

`tryAAConformanceSuffix` handles `s<word-compressed-proto><conformance-module>S<letter>R<subject>rlMc`
patterns (e.g. `s0A18CollectionProtocolsSlRzrlMc` = LazyCollectionProtocol + Collection req on A).

Before: blind scan found `rl` before `Mc` and set `foundCondReq=true`, but `condPrefix=""` because
no structured parsing was done. Output was missing `< where A: Swift.Collection>` prefix.

Fix: Replace blind-scan-only with structured `S<letter>R<subject>` parsing (same loop as
`tryStdlibProtoConformanceSuffix`). When parsing succeeds with `rl` terminator and
`conformanceIsSwift && !isConcurrency`, build `< where A: Swift.Protocol>` prefix.

Symbols fixed: LazySequence, LazyMapSequence, LazyFilterSequence, LazyDropWhileSequence,
LazyPrefixWhileSequence, ReversedCollection (LazySequenceProtocol), Slice (LazySequenceProtocol),
plus Dictionary (_HasCustomAnyHashableRepresentation with B: Hashable).

### Fix 2: tryConformanceDescriptorMc — ObjC __C types in Foundation conformances (+4)

`uiTypeMods = {"SwiftUI", "UIKit", "Combine", "__C"}` caused ObjC types conforming to Foundation
protocols to use simplified output (just type name, no `: Protocol in Foundation`).

When `typeMod == "__C" && modName == "Foundation"`, use full qualified format.

Symbols fixed: NSObject conformances to _KeyValueCodingAndObserving,
_KeyValueCodingAndObservingSequence, _KeyValueCodingAndObservingPublishing, and
NSData : Foundation.DataProtocol.

### Fix 3: tryStdlibProtoConformanceSuffix — <A where A:...> vs < where A:...> for Foundation (+2)

In the constraint prefix builder (line ~1188), the `<subjects where constraints>` form was only
used for `moduleName == "Swift"` non-conditional non-assoc-type conformances. Foundation simple
(`l`-terminated, not `rl`) conformances were always using `< where constraints>` form.

Fix: Remove the `moduleName == "Swift"` guard — use `<A where A:...>` form whenever
`!hasAssocType && !condReq`, regardless of module.

Symbols fixed: Foundation.PredicateExpressions.Value<A> : Swift.Encodable in Foundation,
Foundation.PredicateExpressions.Value<A> : Swift.Decodable in Foundation.

